   "solution": "Let $a_1,\\dots,a_q$ be the columns of $A$. Each $a_j\\in\\operatorname{col}A$, and the columns of $X$ span $\\operatorname{col}A$, so $a_j$ is a linear combination of the columns of $X$: $a_j=Xy_j$, where $y_j\\in\\mathbb{F}^r$ is its coefficient vector. Then\n$$A=[a_1\\,\\cdots\\,a_q]=[Xy_1\\,\\cdots\\,Xy_q]=X[y_1\\,\\cdots\\,y_q]=XY,\\qquad Y\\in M_{r\\times q}.$$"
