   "solution": "$Y$ has full row rank $r$, so its rows are independent. Every linearly independent list in a finite-dimensional space can be extended to a basis, by adjoining standard basis rows $e_j^T$ that are not in the current span until there are $n$ vectors. Then $\\begin{bmatrix} Y \\\\ Y_2 \\end{bmatrix}$ is $n\\times n$ with $n$ linearly independent rows. So it has rank $n$ and is invertible."
