   "answer": "$\\operatorname{rank} A = 4$.",
   "solution": "$A$ has 4 rows, so $\\operatorname{rank} A \\le 4$. The $4\\times 4$ submatrix formed by the first four columns,\n$$\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5 & 0 \\end{bmatrix},$$\nhas determinant $-97 \\neq 0$, so the first four columns of $A$ are linearly independent and $\\operatorname{rank} A \\ge 4$. Hence $\\operatorname{rank} A = 4$."
