   "problem": "H1008-08",
   "problemTitle": "Problem 8",
   "part": "",
   "type": "construct",
   "scope": "MT1",
   "setup": "",
   "context": "",
   "contextLabel": "",
   "text": "Note that the hypothesis that $A$ is full column rank is needed in Problem 6 but is not needed in Problem 7. Show by example that this hypothesis cannot be omitted in Problem 6.",
   "midtermProof": [],
   "answer": "Take $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$ (rank 1, not full column rank), $x_1 = e_1$ and $x_2 = e_2$. Then $Ax_1 = Ax_2 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}$, which is a linearly dependent list.",
